WEBVTT

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.410
The time has come!

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.010
You thirteen who guard the stories,

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.410
if you object to the banquet, then speak up.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:26.350
We do not object.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:27.390
Then...

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.670
The Hexennacht will be held.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:19.740
The Origin Ramayana shows the future.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:23.690
I already know that you're going to lose.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:25.700
I see.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.720
What a coincidence.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:33.850
Hop, hop, hop!

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:35.710
What are you doing?

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.800
I read a book that said

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.290
if you do this, it lowers your 
center of gravity and relaxes you.

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:44.690
It's time to go!

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:49.730
The first match started
 less than three minutes ago.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:01.120
Impossible...

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:05.190
This can't be!

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:15.710
Mahakali, you said 
you know the future, right?

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:19.090
But the future is ever-changing.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:22.160
I can see all its possibilities.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.140
The winner is the German School!

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:44.590
Let's concentrate on our match for now.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.900
There's the problem girl.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:52.960
Yes.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:01.460
Ceremonial Magic: Hexennacht!

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:09.550
I want to grant the wishes 
of everyone in the Russian school.

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:12.350
But for Shizuka-chan's sake, I...

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:16.660
For the sake of Shizuka-chan, 
who granted my wish to be her friend,

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:19.770
I can't lose this, no matter what!

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:27.680
The ancient tale of Cinderella, rewritten!

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.410
Unacceptable!

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:34.050
And then there's the fact that you let 
someone from the other world make a contract...

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:38.880
I can't sleep for fear of what might 
happen to Cinderella's Origin!

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:45.470
Both sides, enter the magic 
circle if you're ready.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:52.210
It's cold!

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:56.100
So it's a tundra stage this time?

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:59.090
Looks like luck isn't on our side today.

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:04.320
Stories are optimized for 
the land in which they're told.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:08.240
The Russian School's Origins

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:13.370
are probably best adapted 
for this environment.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:17.400
It's safe to say, we're at a disadvantage.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:23.460
Altering the choice of the 
Scriptures of Earliest Ancestor?

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:27.850
If the Japanese school loses, 
we can take Cinderella.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:30.080
I don't like it.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.510
It's necessary,

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.760
if we want to protect an ancient Origin.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:35.600
You see?

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:40.060
Let your power dwell 
within me, Moon Princess!

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:43.530
Here I go! Little One-Inch!

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:47.240
Let's go! The Grateful Crane!

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.700
Cinderella Doesn't Look Back!

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:13.150
Bad luck won't stop us.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:15.540
Let's go, everyone!

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.580
She's flying!

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:24.610
The magic of the Vampire Origin, Flight!

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.030
And...

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:28.720
Weather Manipulation!

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:36.540
What's all this snow for?

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.660
Don't let your guard down, no matter what!

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:40.120
Right!

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:49.820
It's over?

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:51.000
Fool!

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:55.290
The true terror of Upierzyca's 
weather comes later.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:58.330
In other words... You'll catch a cold!

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:00.480
Yay! We won!

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:03.170
Now, if you don't want to catch a cold,

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:06.100
surrender, so you can warm up!

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:08.170
Colds are no fun!

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.650
Your nose gets runny, 
you lose your appetite,

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.030
and you get a headache, too!

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.990
I'm getting a headache for another reason.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:15.950
Magic Mallet!

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:21.500
Hurry up and catch a cold!

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.670
Catch it now!

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:25.170
Feather Cloth!

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:40.990
"Stalin is a fool!"

00:07:43.010 --> 00:07:46.180
A man yelled in Red Square.

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:53.430
He was arrested by the secret police 
and sentenced to twenty-five years.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:57.850
He was given five years
 for insulting the head of state,

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.970
and twenty years for revealing 
classified information!

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:13.720
The magic of the Origin, 
The Princess Who Never Smiled,

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.260
Roar of Laughter.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:18.610
The worse the joke, the more powerful it is!

00:08:18.610 --> 00:08:22.620
I can't move!

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:27.950
What would happen if they adopted 
communism in the Sahara Desert?

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:30.640
They would run out of sand!

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:36.450
The Russians enjoy vodka 
like the British enjoy tea.

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:39.970
There's a whole vodka infrastructure,

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:43.840
and if you turn the knob, 
vodka comes out of the faucet.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:50.120
Just hearing the word 
"Russia" makes me laugh!

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:52.220
It's so funny!

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:55.060
Oh no, Mai...

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:56.800
She died of laughter!

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.970
No, I'm not dead!

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:02.270
Come forth, Comrade Nadia.

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:08.260
Origin: The Mitten!

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:13.180
The Mitten's Total Absorption!"

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:15.610
If she touches us...

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:17.310
My stomach...

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:19.770
I can't dodge!

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.200
What?

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:28.960
I stopped laughing?

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:31.120
What's wrong?

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:33.500
Comrade Eva, keep the spell up!

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:36.560
I-I'm out of jokes...

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:40.890
I carefully selected them 
from my funniest jokes,

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:42.540
so there aren't that many...

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:46.080
They weren't that funny, anyway!

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.820
Robe of the Fire Rat!

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:56.420
I can't move!

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:09.030
Your bodies are now

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:13.050
under the control of the 
The Gigantic Turnip, Enforced Cooperation!

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:16.000
We're moving...

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:17.640
...in...

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:19.340
...sync!

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:21.380
That's how it works.

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:22.210
Now, then.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:25.640
Hop, hop.

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:27.520
Hop, hop.

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:28.940
Hop, hop.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:35.320
No!

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:38.110
You lose.

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:43.740
Kasumi-san!

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:46.240
Ariko-san was sealed!

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:50.620
Enforced Cooperation... a powerful spell.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:55.510
If we couldn't approach them 
under the cover of the blizzard,

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:58.470
we wouldn't have been able to take 
them all out at once like this.

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:01.550
Curse your bad luck, Japanese School!

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:05.300
Castle!

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:16.200
Dolls, do something!

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:22.130
We did! We won!

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:24.180
We've won!

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:34.060
Maria...

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.210
Robe of the Fire Rat!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:43.960
Wake up, comrade!

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.090
Shizuka-chan, now!

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:56.900
Jeweled Branch of Horai!

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:01.240
I'm sorry, Comrade Tatiana!

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:22.590
Is this...

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:24.590
Tatiana-san's Origin,

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:26.530
Ivan the Fool...

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:32.270
Yes.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:34.290
The Joy of Physical Labor.

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:38.380
Not just the Japanese school's,

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:42.040
but everyone's Buchhülle vanished.

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:44.300
Who wins, then?

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:46.010
No one.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:51.220
Can we say that both lost?

00:12:52.490 --> 00:12:53.010
No object—

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:54.020
I object!

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:56.010
How rude!

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:57.770
I'm sorry.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:13:00.710
But I believe the match should be continued.

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:01.890
Get out of here!

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:04.410
No one's asking you!

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:07.780
Would you object to the 
Committee's decision, then?

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:09.860
Of course not.

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:16.000
But the same thing happened in 
the Hexennacht 300 years ago,

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:21.330
and the Committee at that time 
decided the match would continue.

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:30.470
W-What of it?

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:32.060
Precedent is merely precedent!

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:34.430
Past decisions have no bearing on this!

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:39.060
Modern situations demand modern judgements.

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:41.690
Oh, my! Are you sure?

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:42.600
What?

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:46.390
The Commitee of 13, no,

00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:50.530
all we Origin Masters, 
must put history above all else.

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:54.820
Don't you always speak of 
the good, old traditions?

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.280
Precedent is merely precedent?

00:13:57.280 --> 00:13:59.520
Past decisions have no bearing on this?

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:02.290
Modern situations demand modern judgements?

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:05.750
Would you blaspheme against history?

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:08.460
Now answer me.

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:15.890
So the match is going to continue?

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:17.600
So it seems.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:19.220
I'm so bored.

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:23.960
If Tatiana's Origin were working properly,

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:27.230
the match would've been 
more interesting, but...

00:14:29.020 --> 00:14:30.640
Ivan the Fool.

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:33.300
It's an interesting enough book

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:36.750
that I thought we could 
use it for our mixed media.

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:40.550
But in the end, 
it's just a B-grade trash Origin.

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:43.350
Totally useless in every way.

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:48.570
For these three minutes, 
no magic can be used.

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:51.170
Do we just wait for time to run out?

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:54.030
Or challenge them to a physical fight?

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:59.360
But we maedchen aren't trained 
to fight with our fists.

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:02.880
It could turn into a protracted battle 
where neither side has an advantage.

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:04.770
Um...

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:09.240
I actually have been studying 
karate since I was a kid.

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:11.390
I'm also a fourth dan.

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:12.410
A black belt?

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:14.740
Also, I do some Krav Maga.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:20.370
The martial arts developed in the 
war-plagued nation of late 20th century Israel?!

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:22.750
Hazuki, you know a little 
too much about that.

00:15:23.140 --> 00:15:25.590
Heh, you can't bluff us.

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:30.750
Then we're all masters of Combat Sambo!

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:32.230
Let's go, comrades!

00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:33.740
Wow!

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:40.470
Come on guys, surrender.

00:15:40.770 --> 00:15:43.530
N-Not yet...

00:15:43.530 --> 00:15:45.970
Even without our magic...

00:15:45.970 --> 00:15:48.180
Even if we can't win in a fight...

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:50.270
We still have the power of camaraderie!

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:53.470
The power of friendship!

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:54.990
Ура́!

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.840
Please surrender!

00:15:58.840 --> 00:16:02.500
This is making me look like the bad guy!

00:16:07.990 --> 00:16:11.920
Let's make your wish, no...

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:17.700
Our wish come true!

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:20.720
<i>The wishes of everyone in the Russian school...</i>

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:22.910
<i>Tatiana-san's wish...</i>

00:16:23.780 --> 00:16:27.350
<i>I want to make them come true, 
but I can't lose!</i>

00:16:31.430 --> 00:16:33.270
She still shouldn't be able to use magic!

00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:35.230
That magic again?

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:36.240
What is it?

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:39.430
That's right...

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:42.620
So that's how that magic works.

00:16:43.410 --> 00:16:45.860
Hazuki-san, what are you doing?

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:47.870
That's what I want to know!

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:03.260
Is this...

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:06.600
Did you fix it, Hazuki-san?

00:17:21.090 --> 00:17:24.070
Let your power dwell within me!

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:25.220
Moon Princess!

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:28.230
What's going on?

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:32.790
It seems that Ivan the Fool's magic 
has started to work like it should.

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:33.800
Why?

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:35.970
You fixed the enemy's origin!

00:17:35.970 --> 00:17:37.380
Is your Origin going out of control?

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:38.410
<i>No.</i>

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:41.240
<i>It granted my wish.</i>

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:44.960
<i>My wish to make their wish come true...</i>

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:47.710
<i>Oh, no! It's my fault!</i>

00:17:48.820 --> 00:17:50.670
<i>It's my fault we're going to lose!</i>

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:54.770
Hazuki-san...

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:59.690
I'm sorry, but we're gong to end this.

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:09.110
We swore that we'd make 
Comrade Tatiana's wish come true!

00:18:09.110 --> 00:18:10.580
Ow!

00:18:10.990 --> 00:18:12.080
What's wrong?

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:13.320
Ow...

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:16.600
My head suddenly 
feels like it's going to burst.

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:18.820
Not your stomach?

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:21.450
I think my knee hurts, too!

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:24.630
And my back and my heels and 
my right hand and my index finger

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:27.350
and molars and back and stomach, and um...

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:31.250
Oh, and my mom back home is sick!

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.370
Is this...

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:37.430
And I promised I'd take my aunt 
and uncle and my cat to the hospital!

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:38.770
A lie?

00:18:37.790 --> 00:18:39.520
And um...

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:42.980
I've also got a dentist 
appointment today, too.

00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:47.620
Tatiana is... lying?

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:50.330
So, um... um...

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:53.290
Let's surrender and go home, okay?

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:04.730
We surrender.

00:19:05.460 --> 00:19:07.090
No, you—

00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:11.640
Now that our wish has come true, 
there's no reason for us to surrender.

00:19:11.640 --> 00:19:15.660
Comrade Tatiana was willing 
to lie to let you win.

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:18.330
We've never seen her so smart before.

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:23.060
Your foolish honesty fixed her stupidity.

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:25.080
Thank you.

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:27.030
We win?

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:29.920
Are you really okay with that?

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:32.030
Kagimura Hazuki,

00:19:32.030 --> 00:19:36.110
it would make me happy 
if you won the tournament.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:37.670
Because you're...

00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:40.540
Our comrade!

00:19:53.780 --> 00:19:55.330
Ура́!

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:59.200
Hazuki's stupidity beat 
Tatiana's stupidity...

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:01.680
Can you put it in a nicer way?

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:05.530
The winner is the Japanese School!

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:10.060
Is that allowed?

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:13.660
The strong win, and the weak lose.

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:18.170
And sometimes that's not 
how it works, perhaps.

00:20:18.970 --> 00:20:22.170
What the heck is that weird magic?

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:36.600
I heard the Japanese School won.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:39.540
It doesn't matter who wins the other matches.

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:42.560
We Germans will win the tournament.

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:47.250
This is humiliation...

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:48.490
Now, now.

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:50.880
The losing teams have to help 
run the tournament.

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:52.530
Those are the rules.

00:20:52.870 --> 00:20:55.490
But that outfit looks great on you!

00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:56.320
It's so cute!

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:57.460
Does it?

00:20:57.460 --> 00:20:58.940
That's a lie!

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:00.100
You little—

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:03.580
Hey, you!

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:07.060
Stop talking and go get the ground set up.

00:21:07.060 --> 00:21:08.880
And go buy me some soda.

00:21:09.140 --> 00:21:12.000
She's being really bossy...

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.600
I don't think it works for her.

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:19.790
I can see how they beat us.

00:21:21.810 --> 00:21:25.400
You were like a wizard out there.

00:21:26.690 --> 00:21:29.280
You can use magic, too, though...

00:23:06.310 --> 00:23:07.140
It's me, Hazuki!

00:23:07.140 --> 00:23:08.440
It's me, Tatiana!

00:23:08.440 --> 00:23:10.500
Everybody join in: Ура́!

00:23:11.380 --> 00:23:14.210
Bu-bbuu! Tatiana, you're a mess!

00:23:14.800 --> 00:23:16.040
You're gullible.

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:17.670
You're weak.

00:23:17.670 --> 00:23:19.050
You're a wimpy human!

00:23:19.050 --> 00:23:19.900
Wimpy!

00:23:19.900 --> 00:23:22.340
The Hexennacht is a world 
where the strongest wins!

00:23:22.340 --> 00:23:24.750
The minute you let your 
guard down, you're out!

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:25.450
Right!

